  "subject": {
    "id": "neutral-structural-history-bootstrap",
    "type": "DOCUMENT"
  },
  "summary": "Ship the neutral structural-history bootstrap and its packaged protocol artifacts.",
  "why": "A project with a typed graph and no governed history had no route into one that did not borrow a domain fixture. The public facade gains create_structural_history and admit_structural_change over four packaged artifacts: a history binding, a state machine, an admission policy, and an admission check. The failing public-facade test landed before the implementation, and the installed skill now teaches the route. The artifacts are structural only: they carry no domain vocabulary, no Event semantics, and no claim of a stable wire format."
}
